## ghost/internal/portscan

The scanning approach in `ghost/internal/portscan` was informed by
**gomap** (https://github.com/JustinTimperio/gomap), MIT licensed.

What was taken is the shape of the thing — a concurrent connect scan
over an expanded target list — rather than the code itself. What was
deliberately NOT taken is the absence of rate limiting: gomap fans out
as fast as the host allows, which is the one behaviour this package
could not adopt. Engagements are run under an agreed packet rate, and
a scanner that cannot be throttled cannot respect one.

The notice is kept because the debt is real either way.

